[instrumental]

[Intro - Reflectively, ~80 BPM]
[a single unaccompanied voice, quiet and suspended in air, mp]
[the intro motif: three soft stepping notes - up a whole step, sagging back a half step - then floating up a wide sixth to one long held high note]
[the motif states itself, trails into silence, then states itself again, patient as deep time]
[deep cello drones underneath like distant dinosaur calls echoing through the jungle, ancient power awakening]

[Main Theme - tenderly]
[the famous hymn theme enters warm and unhurried, flowing in a gentle six-beat sway]
[hook cell one: a long note on the tonic sung twice, dipping down a half step and rising back home - a slow heartbeat, the signature of the whole theme]
[hook cell two: the same repeated-note dip again, but this time it tips upward one step instead of resolving]
[hook phrase two: the melody lifts to a higher held note, sings it twice, and settles back down one step - the peak of the phrase glowing]
[the answering phrase reaches higher still, harmony blooming warmer and more chromatic beneath it, then eases off, poco ritardando]
[strings and woodwinds weave the theme together - awe, not menace, the first glimpse of a living dinosaur]

[Reverently]
[the noble fanfare strain: stately chords moving in dotted rhythms, short-long, short-long, like a procession]
[each chord placed with reverence, the melody carried on top, majestic and complete]

[Building Statement]
[the hymn theme returns fuller, mezzo-forte, meter breathing freely between six beats and four]
[each phrase a step closer to wonder, brass warming underneath, strings ascending]

[Grand Statement]
[full orchestra fortissimo, the hymn theme in radiant block chords, dinosaurs revealed in all their glory]
[lush strings soar like wings, brass carries the ancient power, the music blossoms like the park itself opening to visitors]

[Bring Out the Melody]
[the theme sings in the middle of the texture while rapid sixteenth-note runs shimmer around it like sunlight on water]
[everyone in the theater feels the wonder of seeing dinosaurs alive, crescendo building]

[Second Peak]
[one more fortissimo statement of the reverent fanfare strain, big rolled chords, percussion rolling underneath]
[then the sound begins to thin, diminuendo, the tour winding home]

[Coda]
[everything falls away quiet, mezzo-forte fading softer, ritardando]
[one last rising arpeggio climbs slowly to a single high held note with a fermata, hanging over a deep sustained bass]
[the note fades like a dinosaur disappearing into the jungle, silence, the park waits for the next tour]
